    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9903" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντίδῐκ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>opponent</i> or
				<i>adversary in a suit,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				2.165
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phdr.</u>
				273c
			</span></i>: fem., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>POxy.</u>
					37i8
				</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iA. D.)</span>: properly, <i>the defendant,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Antipho
				1.2
			</span></i>; but also, <i>the plaintiff,</i> Lys<i><span class="en">
				7.13
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. πρός τινα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antipho
					1.5
				</span></i>
			:—generally, <i>opponent, adversary,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				41
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀληθινῶν ἀ.</span> [<i><span class="en">
				Heraclit.
			</span></i>]<i><span class="en">
				133
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>1 Ep.Pet.</u>
				5.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Ir.</u>
				p.65W.
			</span></i></div>
